; Cram tests of the context rule that need no corpus. A file reached through
; a named include path (`from NAME require`) is checked in the context of the
; entry that reaches it, and an entry in the project root is found from a
; subdirectory of it. Both are the context rule docs/user-guide.md describes,
; over small fixtures each test writes itself, so the tests run on every tree
; and do not depend on JASMIN_CONTEXT_CORPUS.
;
; The binary is declared even though dune would build it anyway: the
; dependency is what makes a rebuilt server re-run these tests instead of
; leaving a recorded pass from the previous binary in place.

(cram
 (deps %{exe:../../../lsp-server/native/main.exe}))
